<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The brand mark at splash size. It holds no geometry: it is drawable/ic_launcher_foreground
  drawn larger, so the mark can never drift between the launcher and the splash the way it
  did when the two pointed at different files.

  The scale is here rather than in the mark itself because the two surfaces want different
  sizes. The launcher foreground is sized against the 72dp window a launcher shows, which
  deliberately leaves room inside the 66dp safe circle; the splash has no such neighbours.
  Android's splash guidance is an icon of 288dp whose content sits inside a 192dp circle —
  two thirds of the canvas, which is a radius of 36 in this drawable's 108 units.

  The mark's own corner reaches 29.34 of 108, so it starts at 82% of that circle. The inset
  is negative, which expands rather than pads: -8% a side scales by 1.16, landing the corner
  at 34.0 (94% of the circle) and the painted grid at 50.1 of 108. Fractions are resolved
  against the bounds the platform hands this drawable, so it follows whatever icon size the
  device uses instead of assuming 288dp.

  Note this figure is not the mark's old one and must not be copied from it. A square mark is
  bounded by its corner where the previous ring was bounded by its edge, so the same -15% that
  suited a ring would push this grid's corner to 38.3 — past the circle, and past the point
  where a splash implementation that does mask would start clipping it.
-->
<inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground"
    android:inset="-8%" />
